# CODEOWNERS
# Automatically requests reviews from the right people/teams when a PR
# touches matching paths. Replace the placeholders below with real
# GitHub usernames or teams (e.g., @your-org/platform-team).
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern in this file wins.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owners for everything in the repo, unless a later match overrides it
* @your-org/maintainers

# Engineering standards & process docs
/README.md @your-org/maintainers
/.github/ @your-org/maintainers

# CI/CD and infrastructure
/.github/workflows/ @your-org/platform-team
/.gitlab-ci.yml @your-org/platform-team
/code-starter/ @your-org/platform-team
/standards/ci-cd-standards.md @your-org/platform-team
/standards/docker-standards.md @your-org/platform-team
/standards/gitops-standards.md @your-org/platform-team

# Security-sensitive files require security team review
/SECURITY.md @your-org/security-team
/.github/dependabot.yml @your-org/security-team
/governance/security-practices.md @your-org/security-team
/governance/risk-management.md @your-org/security-team

# Legal/compliance-bearing files
/LICENSE @your-org/legal-compliance
/LICENSE-DOCS @your-org/legal-compliance
/NOTICE @your-org/legal-compliance
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md @your-org/legal-compliance

# Release management
/CHANGELOG.md @your-org/release-managers

# Restrict who can change review-assignment rules themselves, to prevent a
# team quietly expanding its own ownership/approval authority
/.github/CODEOWNERS @your-org/org-owners
